  "title": "Twists add nothing in three dimensions, and the sign survives them",
  "subject": "Whether twisted or ordered bit laws, or positive weights, let counting see more of a three-manifold",
  "conclusion": "On ordered triangulations with one bit per edge, twists and orientations add nothing: exactly the seven symmetric counting laws survive the ordered moves, so counts see a three-manifold only through its mod-2 first cohomology. Positive Turaev-Viro weights for the Fibonacci and twisted Fibonacci rules cannot have full support and are pure gauge on the parity class: the sign survives the twist.",
